  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The latest beta seems to have broken stop action animation systems.\nTo explain what a stop action system is, consider the most simple version that triggers an audio clip on collision. This system consists of a particle system, an audio source under the particle system, and an always running animation that is setting the particle system on. The particle system is set to not loop, run only briefly, and emit only one particle that exists for a very long time. Its stop action setting is set to disable, meaning that once that one particle dies it will turn itself off. We also set the particle to die when it collides or enters a trigger. Then, on collision with an object, the particle system will turn itself and its child audio source off. The animation will immediately turn the particle system back on. This will cause the audio source to play its sound clip as it has \"play on awake\" checked.\nAs of the beta, the system still kind of works, but now something is trying to turn off the particle system every frame after its stop action has fired for the first time. This fights with the animator trying to turn it back on, and in my simple play audio on collision example it causes the audio to become garbled and repeat randomly. This does not happen in live or unity, so I am sure it is something caused by the changes made in the beta.",
